        "subject": "LU-20276 tests: exclude sanityn/56b due to OOM crash",
        "message": "LU-20276 tests: exclude sanityn/56b due to OOM crash\n\nExclude sanityn.sh test_56b testing on clients with less than 15.5GB\nof RAM until ZFS cache usage is fixed.  This threshold was chosen\nsomewhat arbitrarily, but will skip the current 4GB test VMs and\nhopefully will still allow the test to run and pass with larger OSS.\n\nOtherwise, it regularly causes the OSS to crash with OOM shortly after\ntest_56b deletes the large/sparse test file (in test_70b or test_71a\nusually) while the OST objects are being destroyed.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanityn fstype=zfs\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I47176361339bfccdba3c36c06fb6856055b08698\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68733\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Jian Yu <yujian@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Emoly Liu <emoly@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
